---
title: Calendar schema
description: The openschema/events contract — calendar events, recurrence and availability shared across apps.
---

`openschema/events` describes calendar events on the user's account. Like
[contacts](/docs/neoworks/openschema/contacts), it's queryable structured data rather than
[encrypted media](/docs/neoworks/storage) — apps need to filter by time and compute availability.

## Fields

```toml
[table.events]
columns = [
  { name = "title",      type = "string"   },
  { name = "start_at",   type = "datetime" },
  { name = "end_at",     type = "datetime" },
  { name = "location",   type = "string"   },
  { name = "recurrence", type = "string"   },  # RRULE
  { name = "attendees",  type = "array"    },  # contact ids
]
indexes = [
  { columns = ["user_id", "start_at"] }
]
```

`attendees` references rows in [`contacts`](/docs/neoworks/openschema/contacts).

## Scopes

- `events:read` — read calendar events and availability.
- `events:write` — create and modify calendar events.

## Querying

```sql
SELECT title, start_at FROM events
WHERE user_id = $auth.id
  AND start_at > time::now()
ORDER BY start_at ASC;
```

